From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <mk@verveflux.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Jan 2026 00:13:08 +0530
Subject: Restore canvas noise fingerprinting protection

Restores the canvas noise feature that was removed from Chromium to
provide per-site, per-session deterministic fingerprinting protection.

Implementation:
- Browser side: Generates random session token per BrowserContext and
  derives per-origin tokens using SHA-256 + FNV-1a hashing
- Token flow: NavigationRequest -> RenderFrameHost -> WebViewImpl ->
  Page -> ExecutionContext via mojo IPC
- Renderer side: Applies deterministic noise to canvas readback
  operations (toDataURL, toBlob) using FNV-1a based pixel perturbation
- Always enabled: ContentBrowserClient::ShouldEnableCanvasNoise()
  returns true by default

Key files:
- content/browser/fingerprinting_protection/canvas_noise_token_data.*:
  Browser-side token generation and management
- third_party/blink/renderer/core/canvas_interventions/
  canvas_interventions_helper.*: Renderer-side noising logic
- Mojo interface: page.mojom UpdateCanvasNoiseToken() for IPC

